mentation (iatrogenic risk factor for hypercalcemia)"], "excluded_candidates": ["Chronic myeloproliferative disorder: leukocytosis with normal differential but no marrow infiltration signs", "Sarcoidosis: hypercalcemia and constitutional symptoms without clear tumor evidence", "Cardiac murmur as primary focus: no evidence of congestive failure or valvular urgency"], "alarm_features": ["Unexplained weight loss", "Marked leukocytosis with normal differential", "Hypercalcemia", "Elevated alkaline phosphatase", "Vitamin D toxicity (iatrogenic hypercalcemia possibility)"]}, "branches": {"B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Chronic Myeloproliferative Neoplasm", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.19943330700096326, "posterior": 0.25459992127076897, "danger": 0.4, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["The normal leukocyte differential and elevated alkaline phosphatase are more consistent with chronic myeloid leukemia (CML) than other myeloproliferative disor…"], "evidence_against": ["Absence of splenomegaly or marrow infiltration weakly argues against chronic myeloproliferative neoplasm."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B2.1", "B2.2", "B2.3", "B2.4"], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.7, "interrupt_relevance": 0.3, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism", "representative_diseases": ["chronic myeloid leukemia", "polycythemia vera"]}, "B3": {"id": "B3", "label": "Lymphoproliferative / Plasma Cell Disorder", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.06916016256748195, "posterior": 0.03869392212126344, "danger": 0.6, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["Hypercalcemia and systemic symptoms are more typical of plasma cell disorders (e.g., multiple myeloma) than lymphoid neoplasms."], "evidence_against": ["Normal differential and no lymphocytosis weakly argue a